Note on scope: unlike the sibling `self-check/` directory, this tool is MIT
throughout — code AND documentation. It is meant to be installed inside
companies, and a NonCommercial clause on the README is exactly the kind of
detail that stops adoption at a legal review. Nothing here reveals the tuned
engine, so nothing here needs protecting.

